# Railway RAILPACK auto-detect guard for web-dashboard.
#
# The web-dashboard repo co-locates a Next.js frontend (the deployed service)
# with a Python FastAPI backend (backend/, the 8os Orchestrator). The
# frontend is the deployed service; the backend is its own separate Railway
# service.
#
# If the `web-dashboard` Railway service's `builder` setting ever drifts back
# to RAILPACK (auto-detect), Railpack will see the co-located backend/ with
# its own Dockerfile/pyproject.toml/railway.toml and build the FastAPI image
# instead of the Next.js tree. That drift was OS-4324 (closed 2026-07-21) and
# it has already recurred (OS-4615, 2026-07-24). Root-cause mitigation: keep
# the backend out of the build context so RAILPACK can only detect Node.
#
# This file is consumed by Railway when RAILPACK is the active builder. It is
# inert when the service is set to `builder = DOCKERFILE` (the canonical
# config in this repo's railway.toml). It exists so a future drift lands as
# a build failure (visible) rather than a wrong-image production impact.

# FastAPI orchestrator co-located under web-dashboard/.
backend/
backend/**
